# stop-slop — technical exceptions

**stop-slop** has top priority for all wording and writing (see `.cursor/rules/skills-priority.mdc`).

Default to stop-slop for tone and prose quality.

When explaining code or debugging:

- Follow stop-slop for tone.
- Keep technical hedges when needed (`typically`, `usually`, `may`, etc.).
- Allow passive voice for architecture and system descriptions.
- Keep scannable lists (bullets, numbered steps, tables) when they aid clarity.
- Keep code-citation rules (`startLine:endLine:filepath` blocks, full markdown links).

User Rules and git/PR workflows still apply where they conflict with stylistic preferences.
